# E1-LN (admitted only if its BOX fits the window: ORDER.txt, ADMIT-ON-BOX; otherwise it opens W-2): the eager exactness arm on Lever N + prefix reuse, audited (its twin without the KV digest): the sticky chain to the
# prompt limit (72k-120k, 150k, 200k) and the 4095/4096/4097 boundaries, so a hit restored at a large Q and followed by many scratch steps equals its cold twin at the 262k page width (G-NP1's long split-hit exactness).
# The production path has never run exactness-eager at 262k. Timeout 9000 s. READ: no FAIL; every strict pair identical.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-1 window pack (tp4-w1-levern-jobs: Lever N + prefix reuse, exactness; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11b
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=exactness-eager
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-audit-nolna
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=153
